# Messages.
# Format: see data/README.md. Fields:
#   sort:                    sort key (editorial, not used by the program)
#   id:                      message id, used by the program
#   error:                   title of an error message (shown in red)
#   error-revised:           revised error title (not used by the program)
#   info:                    title of an information message (shown in gold)
#   info-revised:            revised info title (not used by the program)
#   text:                    message text; \n is a line break, \l toggles symbol translation, <param> is replaced
#   description:             when the message appears (for the programmer)
#   programmer-note:         comment to the programmer
#   buttons:                 buttons: 'Label:action.Label:action;default-index'

# Instructions for the creation of this file.  Copy the Excel material and paste into this file.  [The following resizing is unnecessary.]  Pull the borders of the table to make them appropriately wide.  Save as Text.
# `s terminates the sort field, used to resort messages according to various criteria.
# `n terminates the message name or message ID
# `d terminates the description of the source for the error (explanation by the programmer)
# `p terminates a comment to the programmer.
# `e terminates the error message (displayed in red by the program)
# `E terminates a revised version of the error message
# `i terminates the information message (displayed in gold by the program)
# `I terminates a revised version of the information message
# `x terminates the explanation (explanation for the user)
# Only one of `e or `i should appear for any message
# Blanks at the start and end of strings are trimmed
# \n forces a carriage return within the text.
# \l toggles conversion of Maggie-talk.  Default is OFF.
# Sort#  `s     Name or ID  `n     Present_Message  P_M_Term     New_Message  N_M_Term     Comment to Programmer  `p     Explanation  `x     Description  `d
sort: 01
id: InvErr001
text: The expression "\l<expression>\l" is not a well formed formula.

sort: 02
id: InvErr002
text: That argument has no conclusion.

sort: 03
id: InvErr003
text: The formula you highlighted, "\l<expression>\l",\nis neither a universal nor an existential\ngeneralization.  Only universal and existential\ngeneralizations can be expanded.

sort: 04
id: InvNot001
text: Please select a problem before switching to a Derivation.

sort: 05
id: InvNot002
text: Please select the size of the universe before expanding.

sort: 06
id: InvNot003
text: Please select a problem and the size of the universe\nbefore switching to a Truth Table.

sort: 07
id: InvNot004
text: Expansion has been disabled for this problem.
